      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1. It\u0027s intentional that this is disabled in Android:\n\n1. As Lee said, we prevent unprivileged bpf program loading in other ways - with selinux.\n2. If this is enabled, then we either have to manually disable it at runtime (defeating the purpose), or grant bpfloader the CAP_SYS_ADMIN privilege, which would be a significant increase in privilege since CAP_SYS_ADMIN gates a great deal of privileged functionality.\n\ni.e. with the current configuration we get the same benefits while keeping the system overall lower privileged\n\nHere\u0027s a more in-depth public description: https://twitter.com/jeffvanderstoep/status/1422771606309335043",
